[
  {
    "sha": "90c98be93632381f447e8d07abe89bf21b67dcd5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDkwYzk4YmU5MzYzMjM4MWY0NDdlOGQwN2FiZTg5YmYyMWI2N2RjZDU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T10:24:55Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T10:24:55Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(gpu): headless compute seam with probe, CPU fallback and binning parity test\n\nAdd the camcraft-gpu crate: the windowless device policy (moved down\nfrom camcraft-ui's headless_gpu, which now re-exports it), a compute\ncapability probe that names \"no compute\" for WebGL2 / GL, one shared\ndevice for each process with a device-lost flag, the\nCAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off switch, and the first kernel: conservative\nfacet binning, the GPU twin of the f64 support facet grid of #2619.\n\nEvery entry answers Result; an Err names the reason, is logged one time,\nand the caller keeps its CPU code. The GPU answer is only a superset\nfilter; the f64 law stays the judge.\n\nThe parity test reads a fixture that camcraft-motion records, so no\ncrate edge joins motion and gpu. xtask gate lists name the new crate.\n\nFixes #2620\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
